    <title>A report on Wiles' Cambridge lectures</title>
    <updated>1994-07-01T00:00:00Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9407220v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/9407220v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>  In lectures at the Newton Institute in June of 1993, Andrew Wiles announced a proof of a large part of the Taniyama-Shimura Conjecture and, as a consequence, Fermat's Last Theorem. This report for nonexperts discusses the mathematics involved in Wiles' lectures, including the necessary background and the mathematical history.</summary>
